agent-ops task task-948d8d00-f572-4f7e-9217-31da5554252e: Criteria advisory config input, effective verifiers and durable reports
intent: Make criteria advisory and task text reflect that typed acceptance criteria already bind every required verifier: render effective verifiers and a non-blocking notice for non-acceptance criteria in mixed tasks; correct the en/zh-TW spec; give the advisor required verifier ids, runner ids/adapters and three fixed rules via a snapshot field excluded from staleness, and send the surface without excluded/dismissed rows; archive each attempt report in the git common dir with worktree fallback; split nonzero reviewer exit into CRITERIA_REVIEW_TARGET_FAILED. No managed template, receipt or config changes.
criteria:
- gate-criterion-notice: In a task that has at least one acceptance criterion, rendered task text (task create, revise, status and export) marks each criterion without acceptance with a notice that it adds no verifier evidence because every required verifier already applies to each acceptance criterion, suggesting to drop it or give it an acceptance binding; a task whose criteria all lack acceptance, or all have it, shows no such notice. The notice is human-readable text only; the task record JSON is unchanged. A node test in tests/task/render.test.ts asserts all three cases.
- effective-verifiers-display: Rendered task text shows an acceptance criterion's Verifiers line as every required verifier (listing any named verifierIds separately) instead of only its own verifierIds, so an acceptance criterion with verifierIds [] no longer renders an empty Verifiers line; a criterion without acceptance still lists exactly its named verifierIds. Asserted in tests/task/render.test.ts.
- spec-required-verifiers: docs/en/spec/acceptance-and-evidence.md and its zh-TW mirror state (EVIDENCE-COMPLETION-001 and the test-count paragraph) that a criterion with typed acceptance needs current PASS evidence from every required verifier whether or not it names them, while a criterion without acceptance needs at least one named required verifier; docs/en/spec/review.md and its zh-TW mirror describe the advisor's verification input, the surface sent without exclusions, and the per-attempt report archive in the git common dir; CHANGELOG.md Unreleased lists the notice, effective verifier display, advisor config input and durable advisory reports. npm test (including the docs translation/spec checks) passes.
- advisor-config-input: The criteria advisory snapshot carries verification {requiredVerifierIds, runners [{id, adapter}]} from the effective config (null when config is unavailable) and a top-level surface without excluded and dismissed rows; the prompt states the 2-5 criteria limit, that every required verifier already applies to each acceptance criterion, and that a check binding needs a listed runner, otherwise recommend review-only or a limitation; neither verification nor surface affects staleness, so a report written before this change is not marked stale. Asserted by node tests in tests/review/criteria.test.ts.
- advisory-durable-diagnosable: When the CLI resolves the git common dir, each finished advisory attempt is written (mode 0600) to <git-common-dir>/agent-ops/criteria-advisory/<task-id>-<attempt-id>.json and survives worktree removal, while the latest report and lock stay in the worktree .agent-ops/reviews; without a common dir the attempt file stays in the worktree as before and the review does not fail. A reviewer process that exits nonzero reports NOT_RUN CRITERIA_REVIEW_TARGET_FAILED, while unusable output from a successful exit stays CRITERIA_REVIEW_INVALID_RESULT. Asserted by node tests in tests/review/criteria.test.ts.
